From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 06:44:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 045/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-common: fix CSIPHY
 analog rail voltages

camss enables vdda-phy and vdda-pll with regulator_bulk_enable and never
requests a voltage, so both rails come up at the bottom of whatever range
the device tree allows. That left vdda-pll (vreg_l3c) at 1144000 and
vdda-phy (vreg_l4a_0p88) at 824000, measured in sysfs, against the
1200000 the downstream CSIPHY node asks for via csi-vdd-voltage and the
0.88V that vreg_l4a_0p88 is named after.

Raise the minimums so the rails come up at the voltages the CSIPHY
expects.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi     | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index eecf968d4..87ae63254 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -255,7 +255,12 @@ vdda_qrefs_0p9:
 		vdda_ufs_core:
 		vdda_usb_ss_dp_core:
 		vreg_l4a_0p88: ldo4 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <824000>;
+			/*
+			 * Same story as vreg_l3c above: this is vdda-phy for the
+			 * CSIPHYs, nothing requests a voltage, and the rail sat at
+			 * 824000 despite being the 0.88V rail its name says it is.
+			 */
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <880000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <920000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 			regulator-allow-set-load;
@@ -424,7 +429,15 @@ vdda_ufs_1p2:
 		vdda_usb_ss_dp_1p2:
 		vddpx_10:
 		vreg_l3c_1p23: ldo3 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1144000>;
+			/*
+			 * This rail feeds vdda-pll of every CSIPHY (and the DSI,
+			 * UFS and USB 1.2V aliases above). camss only enables its
+			 * supplies, it never requests a voltage, so the rail came
+			 * up at the bottom of this range - 1144000, measured. The
+			 * downstream CSIPHY node asks for 1200000
+			 * (csi-vdd-voltage), so start there.
+			 */
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1256000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 			regulator-allow-set-load;
